printf reads our input as format string
         ↓
prints address (4 bytes) + 134513824 spaces = 134513828 chars total
         ↓
%4$n → reads position 4 → finds 0x08049838 (exit@GOT)
     → writes 134513828 (= 0x080484a4) into 0x08049838
         ↓
exit@GOT now contains address of o()
         ↓
program calls exit(0)
→ looks up exit@GOT → finds 0x080484a4
→ jumps to o() instead of real exit()
         ↓
o() calls system("/bin/sh") → shell as level6! 🎉

